{{Navbar modding}}
{{Page version|42.22.0}}
<translate>
<!--T:1-->
A '''Lua event''' in programming is a signal or notification that something has occurred or changed. In {{ll|Project Zomboid}}, most often a modder's custom functions are attached as observers to an event, so they'll run when the event is called.

A full list of the Lua events can be found in:
* [[:Category:Current Lua events|Lua events category]]
* {{ll|LuaDocs}}

== Hooking to an event == <!--T:4-->

<!--T:5-->
To hook a function to an event, you use the <code>Events</code> object. For example, to hook a function to the <code>OnCreatePlayer</code> event, you would write:
</translate>
{{CodeSnip
| lang = lua
| code =
Events.OnCreatePlayer.Add(yourFunction)
}}

<translate>
<!--T:6-->
<code>yourFunction</code> is a reference to your Lua function. By using this same reference, you can also remove the function from the event:
</translate>
{{CodeSnip
| lang = lua
| code =
Events.OnCreatePlayer.Remove(yourFunction)
}}

<translate>
<!--T:7-->
Your function needs to have parameters that match the event's output. For example, the <code>OnCreatePlayer</code> event has the parameter <code>player</code>. Your function would need to be:
</translate>
{{CodeSnip
| lang = lua
| code =
local function yourFunction(player)
    -- your code here
end
}}

<translate>
<!--T:8-->
Each events listed in
</translate> [[:Category:Current Lua events|Lua events category]] <translate><!--T:9-->
have example code snippets to show how to hook a function to them and their various parameters.

== List of events triggered on game start == <!--T:10-->

<!--T:11-->
The list below is a list of events that are triggered when loading into game, ''in the order in which they are triggered.''

<!--T:12-->
'''Launch Game'''
* {{ll|OnLoadSoundBanks}}
* {{ll|OnGameBoot}}

<!--T:13-->
'''Start new game/load game/connect to server'''
* {{ll|OnPreMapLoad}}
* {{ll|OnPreDistributionMerge}}
* {{ll|OnDistributionMerge}}
* {{ll|OnPostDistributionMerge}}
* {{ll|OnInitWorld}}
* ''Sandbox Options loaded here''
* {{ll|OnLoadedTileDefinitions}}
* {{ll|OnLoadRadioScripts}}
* {{ll|OnInitGlobalModData}}
* {{ll|OnLoadMapZones}}
* {{ll|OnLoadedMapZones}}
* {{ll|OnNewGame}} - Client only
* {{ll|OnGameTimeLoaded}}
* {{ll|OnSGlobalObjectSystemInit}} - Basically right before the Click to Start screen
* {{ll|OnServerStarted}} - Server only

<!--T:14-->
'''Click to Start screen here''' - running heavy functions on the following events is the cause for freezing after clicking to start.
* {{ll|OnCreatePlayer}} - Client only
* {{ll|OnGameStart}} - Client only
* {{ll|OnLoad}} - Client only

== Custom events libraries == <!--T:15-->

<!--T:16-->
Below are different libraries that add custom events to the game for modders to hook functions to in the same way as vanilla events.
* {{ll|Events Plus API}} by Dismellion
* {{ll|Starlit Library}} by Albion
* {{ll|Doggy's Library}} by SimKDT
* {{ll|Vehicle Events API}} by Konijima

